<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Philippine–American War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1899">1899</a>–<a href="/years/1902">1902</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Philippine–American War was fought between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and the First Philippine Republic after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> ceded the islands to the United States in 1898. Fighting broke out in February 1899, and Filipino forces turned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> warfare. The United States declared it over in 1902 after the capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emilio-aguinaldo">Emilio Aguinaldo</a>, though resistance continued for years and many thousands of Filipino civilians died.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/philippine-american-war.jpg" alt="Philippine–American War" width="320" height="223" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Perley Fremont Rockett · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Manila646_1899.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
